 [17592186399373 1081 "$(-3,1)$ and $(3,5)$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399373 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399373 1084 #uuid "3d165dca-76a6-5440-b19b-8c808cb523b0" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399374 1081 "$(1,3)$ and $(1,5)$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399374 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399374 1084 #uuid "523960b9-215b-5ec5-9e2e-830b99e6b9c5" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399375 1068 #edb/ref 17592186399376 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399375 1069 "q-51432" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399375 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399375 1071 "![](images/0c/0c8969fae3e21c8e5f5019509636e2307211921d742e6f067d9ee1c50499541b.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the function $y=f(x),$ defined on $[-3,3].$ Find the intervals on which the function $f(x)$ is concave up." 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399375 1072 #uuid "b1beed24-efd2-587e-8b4f-b044374db684" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399375 1074 "The concavity of a function refers to the direction in which its graph curves.\n\n- If the graph curves upward, like a \"smile\" ($⌣$), then the graph is said to be *concave up*.\n\n- If the graph curves downward, like a \"frown\" ($⌢$), then the graph is said to be *concave down*.\n\nIt's helpful to remember the mnemonic \"concave down like a frown.\"\n\nWe can see that the function is curved upwards like a smile ($⌣$) over the intervals $(-3,-1)$ and $(1,3).$\n\n![](images/ae/ae9ce6ca2597a4d5d1ca150c1e97d7c7a0a35f59fe5d6421b75203c6882d2052.png)" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399376 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399377 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399376 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399378 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399376 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399379 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399376 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399380 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399376 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399381 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399376 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399376 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399376 1079 #edb/ref 17592186399381 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399376 1080 #uuid "38c59fe2-2779-5ba6-9c0d-69d20ff0ea27" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399377 1081 "$(-3,0)$ only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399377 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399377 1084 #uuid "0e973d9a-0f09-5900-bf22-eef66722e865" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399378 1081 "$(1,3)$ only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399378 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399378 1084 #uuid "47cac611-9920-5c71-952f-dd8cb39ccdf9" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399379 1081 "$(-3,-1)$ only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399379 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399379 1084 #uuid "4042983e-d1df-528a-8fe4-25f17290d359" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399380 1081 "$(-1,1)$ only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399380 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399380 1084 #uuid "c7b0f23a-5c95-5614-8f48-1c8705ee4818" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399381 1081 "$(-3,-1)$ and $(1,3)$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399381 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399381 1084 #uuid "f3e429b3-2ae0-5777-a461-216e6c6244c6" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399382 1068 #edb/ref 17592186399383 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399382 1069 "q-52413" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399382 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399382 1071 "![](images/75/75a7f3bfae55a97fbc0c05e2e0356d21de6ceabcc82ac3e1c965838a636f5ecc.png)\n\nWhich of the following systems of inequalities defines the shaded region shown above?" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399382 1072 #uuid "9187138f-ae2f-5a56-952a-6135b67724bf" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399382 1074 "Consider the line $y=3x+1.$ Since the line is solid, the inequality is an \"or equal to\" inequality. Also, since the shaded region lies *above* the line, the inequality is a \"greater than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny\\ge 3x+1.\n$$\n\n    \n\nNow consider the line $y=2.$ Since the line is solid, the inequality is an \"or equal to\" inequality. Also, since the shaded region lies *above* the line, the inequality is a \"greater than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny\\ge 2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the system of inequalities that defines the shaded region is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}y\\ge 3x+1 \\\\ y\\ge 2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399383 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399384 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399383 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399385 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399383 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399386 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399383 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399387 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399383 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399388 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399383 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399383 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399383 1079 #edb/ref 17592186399384 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399383 1080 #uuid "6391aa03-c66c-510d-8de3-714552c986fb" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399384 1081 "{\\begin{aligned}y\\ge 3x+1 \\\\ y\\ge 2\\end{aligned}" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399384 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399384 1084 #uuid "c6c66b28-305f-5672-966e-0edbadb3f68b" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399385 1081 "{\\begin{aligned}y\\ge 3x+1 \\\\ y\\le 2\\end{aligned}" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399385 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399385 1084 #uuid "22d57f63-0dab-54f1-a015-47cd4fa3ad27" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399386 1081 "{\\begin{aligned}y\\ge 3x+1 \\\\ y<2\\end{aligned}" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399386 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399386 1084 #uuid "c282cd0f-a1b4-575a-bd8d-6fbc31f00808" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399387 1081 "{\\begin{aligned}y\\le 3x+1 \\\\ y\\le 2\\end{aligned}" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399387 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399387 1084 #uuid "dcc09857-90e2-5fa6-8e10-a5896664af24" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399388 1081 "{\\begin{aligned}y\\le 3x+1 \\\\ y\\ge 2\\end{aligned}" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399388 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399388 1084 #uuid "076f9837-2705-5d0a-9c57-71c316b16391" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399389 1068 #edb/ref 17592186399390 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399389 1069 "q-52461" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399389 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399389 1071 "![](images/ba/ba01cf5268f2bd62835c925a5eb793c0d98663948899c9e9aba2eeacd37ff30a.png)\n\nWhich of the following systems of inequalities defines the shaded region shown above?" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399389 1072 #uuid "d48a81ca-ca4e-5354-bd11-f73315ba7d7f" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399389 1074 "Consider the line $y=2x+6.$ Since the line is dashed, the inequality is strict. Also, since the shaded region lies *below* the line, the inequality is a \"less than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny<2x+6.\n$$\n\n    \n\nNow consider the line $y=5.$ Since the line is dashed, the inequality is strict. Also, since the shaded region lies *below* the line, the inequality is a \"less than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny<5.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the system of inequalities that defines the shaded region is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}y<2x+6 \\\\ y<5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399390 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399391 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399390 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399392 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399390 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399393 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399390 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399394 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399390 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399395 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399390 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399390 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399390 1079 #edb/ref 17592186399392 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399390 1080 #uuid "057029ec-da64-5909-af01-3dd51581c107" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399391 1081 "{\\begin{aligned}y<2x+6 \\\\ y>5\\end{aligned}" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399391 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399391 1084 #uuid "599f73e4-3ca9-5922-b9a5-51c11d904876" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399392 1081 "{\\begin{aligned}y<2x+6 \\\\ y<5\\end{aligned}" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399392 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399392 1084 #uuid "88ca59a7-54b0-51b6-8e85-e1665efeaa4a" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399393 1081 "{\\begin{aligned}y\\le 2x+6 \\\\ y\\le 5\\end{aligned}" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399393 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399393 1084 #uuid "cc2ec7bb-7f05-5512-a12e-01138a6573c3" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399394 1081 "{\\begin{aligned}y>2x+6 \\\\ y<5\\end{aligned}" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399394 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399394 1084 #uuid "17af44de-3d26-5293-8028-23cd473e2e0b" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399395 1081 "{\\begin{aligned}y>2x+6 \\\\ y>5\\end{aligned}" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399395 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399395 1084 #uuid "b7ebc338-a51c-54a2-9008-89b303d45e94" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399396 1068 #edb/ref 17592186399397 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399396 1069 "q-54202" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399396 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399396 1071 "What is the center and radius of the circle with the equation ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=169?$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399396 1072 #uuid "13dc47a1-270d-56c2-8deb-b105337fbddb" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399396 1074 "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the origin is \n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nSo, the equation ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=169$ represents a circle that is centered at the origin, with radius\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{2} & =169 \\\\ r & =\\sqrt{169} \\\\ r & =13.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we disregarded the negative solution for the radius since the radius of a circle must be positive.\n\nTherefore, the circle is centered at $(0,0)$ and its radius is $13.$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399397 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399398 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399397 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399399 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399397 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399400 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399397 1075 