436 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399436 1084 #uuid "f0a7de99-c75b-55c2-bfe2-679645b43eb4" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399437 1068 #edb/ref 17592186399438 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399437 1069 "q-62825" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399437 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399437 1071 "A tank has an inlet and an outlet. When the inlet is turned on, the rate at which water flows into the tank governed by the function\n\n$$\nr(t)=9{t}^{2}+18,\n$$\n\nwhere $r(t)$ is measured in liters per minute and $t>0$ is the time in minutes.\n\nWhen the outlet is switched on, water leaves the tank through it at a rate of $14$ liters per minute.\n\nThe inlet is switched on, and the water level increases to $120$ liters, at which point the outlet is also switched on. How much water is in the tank $10$ minutes after switching on the outlet, given that the outlet is switched on at $t=0?$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399437 1072 #uuid "d586afc6-dd55-5a3f-a72a-36aae91b1948" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399437 1074 "Water enters the tank at a rate of $9{t}^{2}+18$ liters per minute and leaves at a rate of $14$ liters per minute. Therefore, the **rate of change of volume** (call it $R(t)$) is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(t) & =r(t)-14 \\\\  & =9{t}^{2}+18-14 \\\\  & =9{t}^{2}+4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the **total volume** of water in the tank after $t$ minutes (call it $T(t)$), we apply the second fundamental theorem of calculus:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(t) & =T(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{t}R(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =120+{\\int }_{0}^{t}(9{x}^{2}+4)\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo ensure that $T$ is a function of $t$ only, we use a different variable ($x$) for the integration. \n\nTo find out the volume of water after $10$ minutes, we substitute $t=10$ into the above and evaluate.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(10) & =120+{\\int }_{0}^{10}(9{x}^{2}+4)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =120+{[3{x}^{3}+4x]|}_{0}^{10} \\\\  & =120+[(3(10)^{3}+4(10))-(0)] \\\\  & =120+3040 \\\\  & =3\\,160\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399438 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399439 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399438 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399440 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399438 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399441 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399438 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399442 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399438 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399443 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399438 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399438 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399438 1079 #edb/ref 17592186399443 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399438 1080 #uuid "31fad44a-2df1-5489-abcd-c6f3bbfc46a2" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399439 1081 "$3\\,020$ liters" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399439 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399439 1084 #uuid "4e4d353e-3cdf-51e1-9b07-e23aab389446" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399440 1081 "$3\\,140$ liters" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399440 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399440 1084 #uuid "2473a95c-bc78-544c-ba5f-dd05a6bde4c3" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399441 1081 "$350$ liters" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399441 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399441 1084 #uuid "d1b5c16a-3e3a-56c0-92e2-62eb6e146444" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399442 1081 "$250$ liters" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399442 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399442 1084 #uuid "ae9877a7-08c8-5095-8bfe-0888fe2d868a" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399443 1081 "$3\\,160$ liter