0f3369" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399499 1081 "III" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399499 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399499 1084 #uuid "ccaa6bd8-19ca-50f7-afe3-f13abc30ccd2" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399500 1081 "IV" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399500 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399500 1084 #uuid "2c6b6c4f-6ff5-5186-9c43-254f26013671" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399501 1081 "Between quadrants II and III" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399501 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399501 1084 #uuid "b616503f-5c11-5640-98b1-3558d18557b5" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399502 1081 "I" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399502 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399502 1084 #uuid "f41f9c75-55f9-59f2-9b27-7b3d50783eb7" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399503 1068 #edb/ref 17592186399504 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399503 1069 "q-64701" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399503 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399503 1071 "Consider the equation ${y}^{″}-2{y}^{′}-15y=0$ where $y=y(t).$ If $y={e}^{\\lambda t}$ is a solution, then $\\lambda =$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399503 1072 #uuid "a341ef36-052b-58a5-8e5a-622fd4d5ea6a" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399503 1074 "Assuming $y={e}^{\\lambda t}$ and differentiating $y$ with respect to $t$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda t},\\,{y}^{″}={\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda t}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda t}-2\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda t}-15{e}^{\\lambda t} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{\\lambda t}({\\lambda }^{2}-2\\lambda -15) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation is therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}-2\\lambda -15 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFactoring the auxiliary equation results in\n\n$$\n(\\lambda +3)(\\lambda -5)=0,\n$$\n\nand so the solutions of the auxiliary equation  are $\\lambda =-3$ or $\\lambda =5.$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399504 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399505 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399504 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399506 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399504 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399507 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399504 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399508 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399504 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399509 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399504 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399504 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399504 1079 #edb/ref 17592186399506 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399504 1080 #uuid "9aa513b8-ca41-5963-9d1c-ec92073b4073" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399505 1081 "$3$ or $-5$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399505 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399505 1084 #uuid "aa7b08f4-fd50-5010-9da5-db54d62d9cfb" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399506 1081 "$-3$ or $5$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399506 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399506 1084 #uuid "4baca1b8-62e7-5f52-af30-1fc3884ec93d" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399507 1081 "$-3$ or $1$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399507 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399507 1084 #uuid "989a9e5a-82d4-559e-b64e-15fdf78c6beb" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399508 1081 "$3$ or $4$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399508 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399508 1084 #uuid "fdbdf5da-2897-576f-842c-af25e23e73b3" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399509 1081 "$-6$ or $4$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399509 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399509 1084 #uuid "e4a7a515-e8e3-5996-959a-f3908110ac5b" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399510 1068 #edb/ref 17592186399511 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399510 1069 "q-64953" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399510 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399510 1071 "Given that ${y}_{1}(x)={e}^{x}$ is a solution to the equation ${y}^{″}-2{y}^{′}+y=0,$ use reduction of order to find a second solution ${y}_{2}(x)$ to the equation." 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399510 1072 #uuid "f0b4e05c-493c-513f-8d82-76dddaa02634" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399510 1074 "According to the reduction of order method, we let ${y}_{2}=u(x){e}^{x}.$ \n\nDifferentiating the above with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{2}^{′} & ={u}^{′}{e}^{x}+u{e}^{x}={e}^{x}({u}^{′}+u) \\\\ {y}_{2}^{″} & ={e}^{x}({u}^{″}+2{u}^{′}+u).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x}({u}^{″}+2{u}^{′}+u)-2{e}^{x}({u}^{′}+u)+{e}^{x}(u) & =0 \\\\ {e}^{x}({u}^{″}+2{u}^{′}+u-2{u}^{′}-2u+u) & =0 \\\\ {e}^{x}{u}^{″} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince ${e}^{x}\\ne 0$ we must have\n\n$$\n{u}^{″}=0.\n$$\n\nLet $w={u}^{′}.$ Then our equation becomes\n\n$$\n{w}^{′}=0\\,⟹\\,w={c}_{1}.\n$$\n\nBut since $w={u}^{′},$ we have\n\n$$\n{u}^{′}={c}_{1}\\,⟹\\,u={c}_{1}x+{c}_{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our expression for ${y}_{2}(x)=u{e}^{x}$ becomes\n\n$$\n{y}_{2}(x)={e}^{x}({c}_{1}x+{c}_{2}).\n$$\n\nFinally, setting ${c}_{1}=1$ and ${c}_{2}=0,$ we get\n\n$$\n{y}_{2}(x)={e}^{x}\\cdot x=x{e}^{x}.\n$$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399511 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399512 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399511 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399513 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399511 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399514 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399511 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399515 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399511 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399516 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399511 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399511 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399511 1079 #edb/ref 17592186399514 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399511 1080 #uuid "ea86f69a-d990-5653-ae40-c11a11e9a47b" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399512 1081 "{y}_{2}(x)={e}^{x}" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399512 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399512 1084 #uuid "a4fd239d-c7ac-543b-9af2-dff66d73ae14" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399513 1081 "{y}_{2}(x)=x" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399513 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399513 1084 #uuid "d7a82ac0-c0b1-522e-87c4-1a14814f3bc8" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399514 1081 "{y}_{2}(x)=x{e}^{x}" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399514 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399514 1084 #uuid "77412101-bb3d-58bf-a714-56bc3f99924a" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399515 1081 "{y}_{2}(x)=\\frac{1}{x}" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399515 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399515 1084 #uuid "686aa6c6-ecea-5827-a8b9-ee253c9c74ee" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399516 1081 "{y}_{2}(x)={e}^{2x}" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399516 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399516 1084 #uuid "20044cf4-5820-566d-9d4e-d2e750da3ea4" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399517 1068 #edb/ref 17592186399518 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399517 1069 "q-65012" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399517 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399517 1071 "Which of the following systems is a boundary value problem?\n\nI. ${y}^{″}+4x{y}^{′}+2y=0,\\,y(0)=-2,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=3$\nII. $4{y}^{″}+y=0$\nIII. $x{y}^{″}+2{y}^{′}-y=0,\\,y(0)=-4,\\,{y}^{′}(1)=-4$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399517 1072 #uuid "b765011e-9d19-55a7-93ef-fd380a1d1bd5" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399517 1074 "If a second-order differential equation for the function $y(x)$ is given with two conditions specified at *different* locations in the domain of $y,$ then this is a **boundary value problem**.\n\nLet's go through each equation in turn.\n\n- The first system is not a boundary value problem. The differential equation is combined with two conditions, but both conditions are given at the same location in the domain of $y(x)$ (i.e., at $x=0$). This is an **initial value problem.**\n\n- The second system is not a boundary value problem. It contains an equation only. No conditions are specified.\n\n- The third system is a boundary value problem. It consists of a differential equation together with two conditions at different points in the domain of $y(x)$ (i.e., at $x=0$ and $x=1$)." 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399518 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399519 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399518 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399520 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399518 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399521 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399518 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399522 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399518 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399523 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399518 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399518 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399518 1079 #edb/ref 17592186399522 131941