-order partial derivatives are continuous on an open set $U,$ the mixed partial derivatives must be equal. Hence, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{yxx}(x,y) & ={f}_{xyx}(x,y) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({f}_{xy}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(y{e}^{xy}(2+xy)) \\\\  & ={y}^{2}{e}^{xy}(2+xy)+{y}^{2}{e}^{xy} \\\\  & ={y}^{2}{e}^{xy}(3+xy).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(1,1):$\n\n$$\n{f}_{yxx}(1,1)=(1)^{2}{e}^{1\\cdot 1}(3+(1)(1))=4e\\,\\,\n$$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399525 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399526 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399525 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399527 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399525 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399528 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399525 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399529 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399525 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399530 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399525 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399525 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399525 1079 #edb/ref 17592186399528 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399525 1080 #uuid "29a5142e-9f89-5edb-9583-bae503ae820a" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399526 1081 "2e" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399526 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399526 1084 #uuid "a7ceb90c-5f78-5aac-95c4-9b929295f4eb" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399527 1081 "2{e}^{2}" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399527 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399527 1084 #uuid "86e71b49-0357-56df-ae34-bbfae281c19a" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399528 1081 "4e" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399528 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399528 1084 #uuid "df88aa45-c9fd-5b07-9a7f-2504e2e6c593" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true